          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "let us express "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 3 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 5 } { 2 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{2}{5}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\frac { 8 } { 2 0 } } ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.125,
            0.846,
            0.144
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "From this we can see that the product is less than both the numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.144,
            0.848,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When do you think the product is greater than both the numbers multiplied, when is it in between the two numbers, and when is it smaller than both?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.198,
            0.848,
            0.276
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "["
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The relationship between the product and the numbers multiplied depends on whether they are between 0 and 1 or they are greater than 1. Take different pairs of numbers and observe their product. For each multiplication, consider the following questions.]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.283,
            0.845,
            0.66
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.154,
                0.283,
                0.845,
                0.66
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_12_table_6.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Situation</td><td>Multiplication</td><td>Relationship</td></tr><tr><td>Situation 1</td><td>Both numbers are greater than 1 (e.g., 43× 4)</td><td>The product (136) is greater than both the numbers</td></tr><tr><td>Situation 2</td><td>Both numbers are between 0 and 1 (e.g., 34 × 25)</td><td>The product (130) is less than both the numbers</td></tr><tr><td>Situation 3</td><td>One number is between 0 and 1, and one number is greater than 1 (e.g., 34 × 5)</td><td>The product (145) is less than the number greater than 1 and greater than the number between 0 and 1</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.672,
            0.847,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Create more such examples for each situation and observe the relationship between the product and the numbers being multiplied."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.718,
            0.847,
            0.759
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ What can you conclude about the relationship between the numbers multiplied and the product? Fill in the blanks:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.774,
            0.846,
            0.813
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• When one of the numbers being multiplied is between 0 and 1, the product is (greater/less) than the other number."
